WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.580
Since Moon Jae-in became president, the
South Korean government has cracked down

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.759
on North Korean defectors raising
awareness of the horrors they endured

00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:15.750
under the Kim regime. North Korea is
responsible for the deaths of millions by

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.710
starvation. It has imprisoned tens of
thousands in political gulags, and Kim

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:23.189
Jong Un arguably runs the cruelest
tyranny in the world. It's no wonder that

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:27.029
each year, more than 1,000 North Koreans
risk their lives to escape. But instead

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:30.720
of praising defectors for highlighting
these abuses, the democratically-elected

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.170
Moon government has chosen to silence
them as part of its policy of rapprochement

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:38.340
with the North. Moon's government has
repeatedly asked defectors to stop

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:43.060
criticizing North Korea as it did during
the 2018 Olympics, but it doesn't stop there.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:45.450
It has allegedly used security services

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:49.079
to spy on defectors; denied their human
rights groups access to government

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:52.379
support; proposed textbook edits that
minimize North Korea's military

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:56.309
provocations; and prevented defectors
from sending information pamphlets about

00:00:56.309 --> 00:00:59.609
South Korea across the border. The goal
of bringing peace to the Korean

00:00:59.609 --> 00:01:03.840
Peninsula is a noble one, but
prioritizing unification over human

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.260
freedom is not the answer.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.560
Do you think South Korea should do more

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:13.500
to support North Korean defectors? Let us
know in our poll. Also, let us know what

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.700
other topics you'd like to see our
scholars cover in 60 seconds, and be sure

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:22.850
to like and subscribe for more research
and videos from AEI.

